{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>So I fell down before HaShem</b> — he says: I was required to fall down on your behalf forty days and forty nights because of this great sin, for at first HaShem said to destroy you, until I pray to HaShem and say: Do not destroy Your people and Your inheritance, for this was his prayer before he descended from the mountain, and from it he was answered with <i>and HaShem relented from the evil which He had spoken of doing to His people</i> (Exodus 32:14). And he did not mention the prayer of the forty days and forty nights, for its measure is longer than the earth and broader than the sea. And the reason for the divine names written with alef-dalet-yod-heh I have already explained (Ramban on Deuteronomy 3:24)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אָלֶ\"ף דָּלֶ\"ת יוֹ\"ד הֵ\"א' refers to the four-letter divine name יהוה spelled out by its component letters; rendered the acrostic literally. The parenthetical cross-reference to Ramban on Deuteronomy 3:24 appears in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:21.622909749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}